<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for Glide Host.app (tools/make-host-app.sh). Deliberately empty:
  every hardened-runtime exception stays off.

  What the host does, and why none of it needs an entitlement:
  - Screen and system-audio capture (ScreenCaptureKit, SCStream with capturesAudio): gated by the
    Screen Recording privacy permission (TCC), not by an entitlement. System audio comes through
    SCStream, not the microphone, so com.apple.security.device.audio-input is not needed.
  - Keyboard and mouse injection (CGEvent posting to the HID event tap) and AXIsProcessTrusted:
    gated by Accessibility (TCC; PostEvent is covered by it).
  - The virtual display: CoreGraphics' private CGVirtualDisplay classes, looked up at run time
    (NSClassFromString) in a system framework. Library validation only restricts loading
    non-Apple, differently signed code; nothing is loaded from outside the app or the OS, so
    com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation stays off. No private symbols are linked.
  - Networking (TCP listen/dial on the LAN, HTTPS to Glide Cloud): not sandboxed, so no network
    entitlements; macOS 15+ asks for Local Network access using NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription.
  - Login item (SMAppService), clipboard, files in ~/Downloads, spawning /usr/bin/open: no
    entitlement.
  - No JIT, no unsigned executable memory, no DYLD_* variables, no debugger attachment, no Apple
    Events: the matching com.apple.security.cs.* / automation.apple-events stay off.

  App Sandbox is not used: a sandboxed app can't post events to other apps or run as the
  per-user LaunchAgent the installers set up.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
